{
  "id": 327799532,
  "iid": 17321,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ieee1905: Fix dissection of the Non-1905 Neighbor Device List TLV",
  "description": "Without this patch, the Non-1905 Neighbor Device List TLV is dissected incorrectly when there are 2 or more non 1905 devices behind a local interface.\n\nIn this case, the local interface MAC is present only once followed by the device MAC.  (see IEEE1905 chapter 6.4.8)\n\nThis is similar as the 1905 Neighbor Device List TLV, which is handled correctly.\n\n=> Lined up implementation of both TLV.\n\nBefore:\n![berfore_patch](/uploads/00aaced76d9f5ac88937c60c55aca958/berfore_patch.png)\n\nAfter:\n![after_patch](/uploads/b08680cb663f671d5979ad94244b23c6/after_patch.png)\n\nExample pcap:\n[non_1905_neighbor_device_list_tlv.pcap](/uploads/c103886860f43ce7b236f636507cedd9/non_1905_neighbor_device_list_tlv.pcap)",
  "state": "merged",
