        {
          "id": 2114671982,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hi,\n\nI changed that line too to make it more logical.\n\nFrom src/epan/proto.h you can see that proto_tree_add_subtree() returns a \"proto_tree\" pointer.\n\n_WS_DLL_PUBLIC proto_tree *\nproto_tree_add_subtree(proto_tree *tree, tvbuff_t *tvb, gint start, gint length, gint idx,\n    proto_item **tree_item, const char *text);_\n\n\nHowever, it does not really make a difference as proto_tree and proto_item are typedef'd to the same thing.\n_/** A protocol tree element. */\ntypedef proto_node proto_tree;\n/** A protocol item element. */\ntypedef proto_node proto_item;_\n\n\nFrederik",
          "author": {
            "id": 22882096,
